          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most basements without a floor drain, the Midea Cube 50-Pint with Pump is the one to buy: about 16 feet of rated lift, ENERGY STAR efficiency and a design that keeps working even if you never use the pump. The Frigidaire is the safe mainstream alternative with a gravity port as a fallback, and the hOmeLabs is the value pick if you test its pump on day one.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you buy, treat the pump as a maintenance item. Keep the hose short and simple, clean the pump screen when you clean the filter and check the discharge point every season. If your space is a crawl space or a basement that stays cold, skip the portables and look at a purpose-built unit instead.
